# No narrative comments

Do not add comments that narrate what code does, restate a bug that was fixed, or explain obvious intent.

```gleam
// ❌ BAD — narrates the next line
// Open the GPIO port
use pins <- result.try(gpio.open() |> ...)
```

```gleam
// ❌ BAD — restates the function
/// Map a Result and log on failure.
fn or_log(...)
```

```gleam
// ✅ GOOD — non-obvious AtomVM / hardware constraint the code alone cannot convey
// Open hardware in this process so `{gpio_interrupt, Pin}` is delivered here.
use pins <- result.try(gpio.open() |> ...)
```

Module docs (`///` / `////`) that describe public API, AtomVM entrypoint contracts, or Orbital packaging are fine. Prefer renaming or restructuring over explaining the obvious.
